/**
{
    "id": "049",
    "category": "Cloud Providers",
    "categorySlug": "cloud-providers",
    "categoryIcon": "cloud",
    "title": "AWS Bedrock",
    "difficulty": "intermediate",
    "icon": "cloud",
    "description": "Chat, stream, and use tools against Claude-on-Bedrock — bearer-token auth or the full AWS credential chain.",
    "guidance": "aiChat( ..., options: { provider: 'bedrock', providerOptions: { ... } } ) routes the request through AWS Bedrock. Authentication resolves in order:\n\n1. Explicit awsAccessKeyId/awsSecretAccessKey/awsSessionToken in providerOptions\n2. AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY / AWS_SESSION_TOKEN environment variables\n3. A Bedrock long-term API key (bearer auth) — explicit providerOptions.bearerToken, or the AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK env var. Opt-in only, never inferred from a plain apiKey.\n4. ECS/EKS container credentials (including EKS Pod Identity's rotating token file)\n5. EC2 IMDSv2 instance-role credentials\n\nBearer-token auth is the simplest option — no SigV4 request signing required.\n\nTool-use and schema-typed structured output are wired up for Claude-family models on Bedrock; requesting either on a non-Claude family throws UnsupportedProviderCapability rather than silently dropping them. Batched HITL approvals (see the Human-in-the-Loop sample) are consistent across OpenAI, Claude, Bedrock, and Cohere.\n\nKnown limitation (3.4.0): Cohere-on-Bedrock is response-side only — replies parse correctly, but the request transform still sends a Claude-shaped body, so Cohere-on-Bedrock chat isn't functional end-to-end yet.",
    "output": "--- Bearer-token auth (simplest — no SigV4 signing) ---\nBedrock says: Hello! I'm Claude, running on AWS Bedrock.\n\n--- Default AWS credential chain (env / container / IMDS) ---\nBedrock says: I can help analyze that dataset — what format is it in?\n\n--- Tool use on Claude-on-Bedrock ---\nTool called: get_account_balance(accountId: acct-9931)\nBedrock says: Your account balance is $4,218.50.\n\n--- Streaming ---\nBedrock is a fully managed service that gives you API access to foundation models from multiple providers...",
    "docsUrl": "https://ai.ortusbooks.com/getting-started/installation/provider-setup.md",
    "provider": "bedrock"
}
*/

// 1. Bearer-token auth — the simplest option, no AWS SigV4 signing required
answer = aiChat( "Say hello and mention what you're running on.", {}, {
    provider       : "bedrock",
    providerOptions: {
        region     : "us-east-1",
        bearerToken: "your-bedrock-bearer-token"   // or set AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK
    }
} )
println( "--- Bearer-token auth (simplest — no SigV4 signing) ---" )
println( "Bedrock says: " & answer )
println( "" )

// 2. Default AWS credential chain — explicit -> env -> ECS/EKS container -> EC2 IMDSv2
chainAnswer = aiChat( "Can you help me analyze a dataset?", {}, {
    provider       : "bedrock",
    providerOptions: { region: "us-east-1" }
} )
println( "--- Default AWS credential chain (env / container / IMDS) ---" )
println( "Bedrock says: " & chainAnswer )
println( "" )

// 3. Tool use — confirmed working for Claude-family models on Bedrock
balanceTool = aiTool(
    "get_account_balance",
    "Look up an account's current balance",
    ( args ) => ( { balance: 4218.50, currency: "USD" } )
).describeArg( "accountId", "The account identifier" )

toolAnswer = aiChat(
    "What's the balance on account acct-9931?",
    { tools: [ balanceTool ] },
    { provider: "bedrock", providerOptions: { region: "us-east-1" } }
)
println( "--- Tool use on Claude-on-Bedrock ---" )
println( "Tool called: get_account_balance(accountId: acct-9931)" )
println( "Bedrock says: " & toolAnswer )
println( "" )

// 4. Streaming
println( "--- Streaming ---" )
aiChatStream(
    "In one sentence, what is AWS Bedrock?",
    ( chunk ) => {
        content = chunk.choices?.first()?.delta?.content ?: ""
        print( content )
    },
    {},
    { provider: "bedrock", providerOptions: { region: "us-east-1" } }
)
println( "" )
